  "notes": [
    "Callback transport is docs-only: the docs show callback URLs carrying paymentID+status+signature and say bKash 'calls' them; the simulator implements a customer-browser GET redirect with no server-to-server POST, since tokenized checkout documents no webhook. send_ipn scenario actions skip with an event.",
    "Business-rule failures answer HTTP 200 with the gateway error shape (house rule, docs-only: samples imply JSON bodies, HTTP statuses unstated). Only malformed JSON gets HTTP 400 from the framework.",
    "Error-code mappings that are simulator choices (all codes real, from payment-error-codes.md): bad/expired token -> 2003, expired paymentId -> 2002, execute-on-failed/cancelled -> 2056, malformed optionals -> 2025. internalCode only with sample-verified values.",
    "Execute pre-condition rejections (2060/2056) do not burn the paymentId; only a completed execution does (2062). Docs say a paymentId 'cannot be reused after an execute attempt regardless of the result' — the simulator reads 'attempt' as an accepted execution (docs-only interpretation).",
    "The grant-token rate limit (2/hour) is not enforced; the token registry is in-memory per process, so restarts invalidate tokens.",
    "productionHosts is empty: no v2 production host is published in the consulted docs.",
    "Agreements, auth & capture and search are out of scope; coupon/agreement/serviceFee response fields are omitted.",
    "Token values (sim_id_*, sim_rt_*), trxId/payerAccount fixtures and the '0011' paymentId infix are simulator choices; shapes follow the doc samples."
  ]
}
